{"meta": {"limit": 100, "next": null, "offset": 0, "previous": null, "total_count": 57}, "objects": [{"abstract": "   The organizational separation between operators of TLS and DTLS\n   endpoints and the certification authority can create limitations.\n   For example, the lifetime of certificates, how they may be used, and\n   the algorithms they support are ultimately determined by the\n   certification authority.  This document describes a mechanism to to\n   overcome some of these limitations by enabling operators to delegate\n   their own credentials for use in TLS and DTLS without breaking\n   compatibility with peers that do not support this specification.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/112723/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-subcerts/", "expires": "2023-01-01T18:17:01Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 332645, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-subcerts", "note": "", "notify": "Joseph Salowey <joe@salowey.net>", "pages": 17, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/332645/", "rev": "15", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/joe@salowey.net/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/108/", "/api/v1/doc/state/112/", "/api/v1/doc/state/17/", "/api/v1/doc/state/116/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2023-05-23T22:02:41Z", "title": "Delegated Credentials for (D)TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   The organizational separation between operators of TLS and DTLS\n   endpoints and the certification authority can create limitations.\n   For example, the lifetime of certificates, how they may be used, and\n   the algorithms they support are ultimately determined by the\n   certification authority.  This document describes a mechanism to to\n   overcome some of these limitations by enabling operators to delegate\n   their own credentials for use in TLS and DTLS without breaking\n   compatibility with peers that do not support this specification.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/112723/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-subcerts/", "expires": "2023-01-01T18:17:01Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 332767, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-subcerts", "note": "", "notify": "Joseph Salowey <joe@salowey.net>", "pages": 17, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/332767/", "rev": "15", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/joe@salowey.net/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/108/", "/api/v1/doc/state/112/", "/api/v1/doc/state/17/", "/api/v1/doc/state/25/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2023-05-25T19:33:58Z", "title": "Delegated Credentials for (D)TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   The organizational separation between operators of TLS and DTLS\n   endpoints and the certification authority can create limitations.\n   For example, the lifetime of certificates, how they may be used, and\n   the algorithms they support are ultimately determined by the\n   certification authority.  This document describes a mechanism to to\n   overcome some of these limitations by enabling operators to delegate\n   their own credentials for use in TLS and DTLS without breaking\n   compatibility with peers that do not support this specification.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/112723/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-subcerts/", "expires": "2023-01-01T18:17:01Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 335304, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-subcerts", "note": "", "notify": "Joseph Salowey <joe@salowey.net>", "pages": 17, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/335304/", "rev": "15", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/joe@salowey.net/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/108/", "/api/v1/doc/state/112/", "/api/v1/doc/state/17/", "/api/v1/doc/state/116/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2023-07-04T01:30:45Z", "title": "Delegated Credentials for (D)TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   The organizational separation between the operator of a TLS server\n   and the certificate authority that provides it credentials can cause\n   problems, for example when it comes to reducing the lifetime of\n   certificates or supporting new cryptographic algorithms.  This\n   document describes a mechanism to allow TLS server operators to\n   create their own credential delegations without breaking\n   compatibility with clients that do not support this specification.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-subcerts/", "expires": "2018-05-03T21:32:52Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 203056, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-subcerts", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 11, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/203056/", "rev": "00", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2017-10-30T21:32:52Z", "title": "Delegated Credentials for TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   The organizational separation between the operator of a TLS server\n   and the certificate authority that provides it credentials can cause\n   problems, for example when it comes to reducing the lifetime of\n   certificates or supporting new cryptographic algorithms.  This\n   document describes a mechanism to allow TLS server operators to\n   create their own credential delegations without breaking\n   compatibility with clients that do not support this specification.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-subcerts/", "expires": "2018-05-03T21:32:52Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 203219, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-subcerts", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 11, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/203219/", "rev": "00", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2017-10-31T19:21:51Z", "title": "Delegated Credentials for TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   The organizational separation between the operator of a TLS server\n   and the certificate authority that provides it credentials can cause\n   problems, for example when it comes to reducing the lifetime of\n   certificates or supporting new cryptographic algorithms.  This\n   document describes a mechanism to allow TLS server operators to\n   create their own credential delegations without breaking\n   compatibility with clients that do not support this specification.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-subcerts/", "expires": "2018-05-03T21:32:52Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 203222, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-subcerts", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 11, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/203222/", "rev": "00", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2017-10-31T20:24:51Z", "title": "Delegated Credentials for TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   The organizational separation between the operator of a TLS server\n   and the certificate authority that provides it credentials can cause\n   problems, for example when it comes to reducing the lifetime of\n   certificates or supporting new cryptographic algorithms.  This\n   document describes a mechanism to allow TLS server operators to\n   create their own credential delegations without breaking\n   compatibility with clients that do not support this specification.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-subcerts/", "expires": "2018-05-03T21:32:52Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 217581, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-subcerts", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 11, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/217581/", "rev": "00", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/2/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2018-05-03T07:16:46Z", "title": "Delegated Credentials for TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   The organizational separation between the operator of a TLS server\n   and the certificate authority that provides it credentials can cause\n   problems, for example when it comes to reducing the lifetime of\n   certificates or supporting new cryptographic algorithms.  This\n   document describes a mechanism to allow TLS server operators to\n   create their own credential delegations without breaking\n   compatibility with clients that do not support this specification.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-subcerts/", "expires": "2019-01-03T23:56:43Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 220511, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-subcerts", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 11, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/220511/", "rev": "01", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2018-07-02T22:56:43Z", "title": "Delegated Credentials for TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   The organizational separation between the operator of a TLS server\n   and the certification authority can create limitations.  For example,\n   the lifetime of certificates, how they may be used, and the\n   algorithms they support are ultimately determined by the\n   certification authority.  This document describes a mechanism by\n   which operators may delegate their own credentials for use in TLS,\n   without breaking compatibility with clients that do not support this\n   specification.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-subcerts/", "expires": "2019-02-18T19:19:26Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 224285, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-subcerts", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 12, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/224285/", "rev": "02", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2018-08-17T18:19:26Z", "title": "Delegated Credentials for TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   The organizational separation between the operator of a TLS endpoint\n   and the certification authority can create limitations.  For example,\n   the lifetime of certificates, how they may be used, and the\n   algorithms they support are ultimately determined by the\n   certification authority.  This document describes a mechanism by\n   which operators may delegate their own credentials for use in TLS,\n   without breaking compatibility with peers that do not support this\n   specification.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-subcerts/", "expires": "2020-05-07T03:04:55Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 251756, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-subcerts", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 15, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/251756/", "rev": "05", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2019-11-04T04:04:55Z", "title": "Delegated Credentials for TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   The organizational separation between the operator of a TLS server\n   and the certification authority can create limitations.  For example,\n   the lifetime of certificates, how they may be used, and the\n   algorithms they support are ultimately determined by the\n   certification authority.  This document describes a mechanism by\n   which operators may delegate their own credentials for use in TLS,\n   without breaking compatibility with clients that do not support this\n   specification.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-subcerts/", "expires": "2019-02-18T19:19:26Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 235096, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-subcerts", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 12, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/235096/", "rev": "02", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/2/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2019-02-18T08:15:52Z", "title": "Delegated Credentials for TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   The organizational separation between the operator of a TLS server\n   and the certification authority can create limitations.  For example,\n   the lifetime of certificates, how they may be used, and the\n   algorithms they support are ultimately determined by the\n   certification authority.  This document describes a mechanism by\n   which operators may delegate their own credentials for use in TLS,\n   without breaking compatibility with clients that do not support this\n   specification.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-subcerts/", "expires": "2019-08-23T22:33:50Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 235145, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-subcerts", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 12, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/235145/", "rev": "03", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2019-02-19T23:33:50Z", "title": "Delegated Credentials for TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   The organizational separation between the operator of a TLS endpoint\n   and the certification authority can create limitations.  For example,\n   the lifetime of certificates, how they may be used, and the\n   algorithms they support are ultimately determined by the\n   certification authority.  This document describes a mechanism by\n   which operators may delegate their own credentials for use in TLS,\n   without breaking compatibility with peers that do not support this\n   specification.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-subcerts/", "expires": "2020-01-09T23:12:38Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 244178, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-subcerts", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 13, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/244178/", "rev": "04", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2019-07-08T22:12:38Z", "title": "Delegated Credentials for TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   The organizational separation between the operator of a TLS endpoint\n   and the certification authority can create limitations.  For example,\n   the lifetime of certificates, how they may be used, and the\n   algorithms they support are ultimately determined by the\n   certification authority.  This document describes a mechanism by\n   which operators may delegate their own credentials for use in TLS,\n   without breaking compatibility with peers that do not support this\n   specification.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-subcerts/", "expires": "2020-05-07T03:04:55Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 251940, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-subcerts", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 15, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/251940/", "r